## Shader Testing Environment

### Files Created

1. **`index.html`** - Main HTML with:
   - All shader source code in `<script type="x-shader/x-fragment">` tags
   - Dropdown selector UI for switching between shaders
   - Import of shader-web-background library

2. **`styles.css`** - UI styling with:
   - Semi-transparent overlay for the shader selector
   - Backdrop blur effect
   - Proper z-indexing to float above the shader canvas

3. **`main.js`** - Shader registry with:
   - `ShaderRegistry.register()` for adding new shaders
   - `ShaderRegistry.start()` for switching shaders
   - Automatic cleanup when switching between shaders

4. **`shaders/gradient.js`** - Simple animated gradient:
   - Single-pass shader
   - Time-based color animation using sin waves
   - Demonstrates basic `iTime` and `iResolution` uniforms

5. **`shaders/feedback-circle.js`** - Feedback loop with trail:
   - Two-pass shader (buffer + image)
   - Orbiting circle with fading trail effect
   - Demonstrates `iChannel0` buffer sampling

6. **`shaders/spectral-feedback.js`** - Spectral color feedback:
   - Two-pass shader with the Zucconi spectral algorithm
   - Creates natural rainbow colors that cycle over time
   - Flowing feedback patterns adapted from xemantic.com

### How to Add New Shaders

To add a new shader, create a file in `shaders/` and register it:

```javascript
ShaderRegistry.register('my-shader', {
  shaders: {
    'my-shader-image': {
      uniforms: {
        iTime: (gl, loc) => gl.uniform1f(loc, performance.now() / 1000),
        iResolution: (gl, loc, ctx) => gl.uniform2f(loc, ctx.width, ctx.height)
      }
    }
  }
}, '<strong>My Shader</strong>Description here.');
```

Then add the corresponding `<script id="my-shader-image">` in `index.html` and an `<option>` in the dropdown.